## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to build a basic, performative list in RN with local data, search, skeleton loading, and rendering optimizations. Also checks understanding of stable item keys and accessibility.

## Key Concepts
- FlatList virtualization
- useMemo and React.memo
- keyExtractor and getItemLayout
- basic accessibility

## Code Example
```javascript
import React, { useMemo, useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import { FlatList, TextInput, View, Text } from 'react-native';

const Item = React.memo(({ name }) => <Text accessibilityLabel={`item-${name}`}>{name}</Text>);

export default function ItemList({ data }) {
  const [q, setQ] = useState('');
  const filtered = useMemo(() => data.filter(i => i.name.toLowerCase().includes(q.toLowerCase())), [data, q]);
  const renderItem = useCallback(({ item }) => <Item name={item.name} />, []);
  return (
    <View>
      <TextInput value={q} onChangeText={setQ} placeholder="Search" accessibilityLabel="search" />
      <FlatList
        data={filtered}
        keyExtractor={item => item.id}
        renderItem={renderItem}
        getItemLayout={(_, index) => ({ length: 48, offset: 48 * index, index })}
        initialNumToRender={20}
      />
    </View>
  );
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you debounce the search input and what would you test for performance?
- How would you enhance accessibility and localization for item text?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests bridging basics, event streams, and hooks with real device APIs, plus practical UI wiring. It introduces platform quirks (Android vs iOS battery APIs) and emphasizes energy impact.

## Key Concepts
- Native modules and TurboModules/JSI bridging
- NativeEventEmitter and React hooks for streaming data
- Platform-specific battery APIs and background threading
- Lightweight UI binding to live data
- Privacy and energy considerations (polling interval, Doze modes)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: useBatteryStream hook (JS side)
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { NativeEventEmitter, NativeModules } from 'react-native';
const { BatteryWatcher } = NativeModules;
const emitter = new NativeEventEmitter(BatteryWatcher);

export function useBatteryStream() {
  const [state, setState] = useState({ level: -1, ts: 0, belowThreshold: false });
  useEffect(() => {
    const sub = emitter.addListener('BatteryUpdate', (payload) => {
      setState(payload);
    });
    return () => sub.remove();
  }, []);
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle rapid battery fluctuations and debounce the events?
- How would you expose a configuration API to skip battery updates when the app is hidden or in the background?
